TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Attributes coral bleaching to ocean acidification, whereas bleaching is primarily driven by thermal stress; this contradicts the later paragraph stating high temperatures cause bleaching."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"Claim that the reef is up to about 250 km wide is unsourced and drives the swath-count conclusion."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"The 2,700 km spacing is along-track between successive orbits; cross-track coverage of a 250 km width requires a repeat-cycle or offset-track analysis, so the five-pass argument is conflated and not properly derived."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"GBRMPA reef facts page [5] is cited for the claim that managers need bleaching maps, which the source does not support."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Bureau of Meteorology capability is cited to a US NOAA page [6], which does not support the Australian agency claim."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"Hand-calculation section does not show the sun-synchronous inclination derivation (only the precession rate), and no STK output is shown to support the claimed agreement."}],"overall":"A well-organised, largely accomplished preliminary report with a clear mission, a logical Gantt-based plan with contingencies, and correct orbital hand calculations. Main weaknesses are a causal error on bleaching, unsourced or mis-cited claims, and a muddled cross-track coverage argument. Marks use the 0-10 descriptor scale.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":32.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Goals, four quantified objectives and named users (GBRMPA, CSIRO/universities, BoM, AIMS operator) are clear, and objectives are traced to user needs. Literature is referenced throughout. Weaknesses: the acidification-causes-bleaching link is technically muddled, and some citations do not support the stated user needs, so the rationale is not fully robust.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Give reef managers direct, repeatable observations of coral colour over the whole Great Barrier Reef"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Objectives 1 and 3 come directly from the managers' need to react within days"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":9.0,"scale":10.0,"points":27.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"The Gantt chart, task descriptions and ordering are logically tied to the mission chain. A risk/trigger/response table provides real contingencies, and information sources are listed. Minor detail gap: the Gantt chart shows Launch Specifics without a clear launch-vehicle decision point, and colour coding is slightly inconsistent with the text.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"the imaging requirements (objectives 1 and 2) fix the orbit altitude and local time, so orbit work comes before ground control"},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Plan fits within the narrative: Contingencies. Week 10 is float as well as editing time"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Hand calculations for period, orbits per day, sun-synchronous inclination and ground-track shift are correct and interpreted against the mission objectives, honestly flagging the coverage trade-off. The STK scenario is only described, with no output shown, and one interpretive claim is unsourced, so progress is strong but not fully evidenced.","evidence":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"Swath at 10 m sampling | 10 m × 6,000 pixels across track | 60 km"},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"A first STK scenario with this orbit has been set up, and its period agrees with the hand calculation."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":16.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear logical structure with headings, labelled figures and tables, and a consistent, professional style. References are numbered in order of first citation. Some citations are attributed to sources that do not support the claim (BoM claim cited to a NOAA page), and the length may exceed the 2-3 page guideline.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Table 2 lists the sources I plan to use and what each is for."},{"where":"Figure 1","quote":"Figure 1: Project Gantt chart, Weeks 2 to 10 (gold = completed, blue = planned, red lines = report deadlines)."}]}]}
